{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ברוך מבנים אשר", :translit "barukh mi-banim asher", :gloss "Blessed from sons Asher"} {:he "כשמכרו השבטים את יוסף", :translit "ke-she-makhero ha-shevatim et yosef", :gloss "when the tribes sold Joseph"} {:he "החרימו שלא יגלו אותו", :translit "hecherimu she-lo yagilu oto", :gloss "they banned that one not reveal him"} {:he "סרח בת אשר ידעה ממכירתו בנבואה", :translit "serach bat asher yad'ah mi-mekhirato be-nevu'ah", :gloss "Serah daughter of Asher knew of his sale through prophecy"} {:he "מפני דשותא דינוקא, או מאבא או מאמא", :translit "mi-penei dishuta dinuka, o me-aba o me-ima", :gloss "because of a child's chatter, either from father or from mother"} {:he "עמדו ונדוהו", :translit "amdu ve-niduhu", :gloss "they arose and excommunicated him"} {:he "ובא מרע\"ה והתירו", :translit "u-va morenu ha-rav ve-hitiro", :gloss "and our master the rabbi came and permitted him"} {:he "כי מנודה אסור בתשמיש המטה", :translit "ki menudeh asur be-tashmish ha-mitah", :loss "for one excommunicated is forbidden in marital relations"} {:he "ברוך מבנים", :translit "barukh mi-banim", :gloss "Blessed from sons"} {:he "יהי רצוי אחיו", :translit "yehi ratzuy echaiv", :gloss "may he be acceptable to his brothers"} {:he "וטובל בשמן רגלו", :translit "ve-tovel be-shemen raglo", :gloss "and he dips his foot in oil"} {:he "ברזל ונחשת מנעלך", :translit "barzel u-nechoshet min'alekha", :gloss "Iron and copper your shoe"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Each phrase of the blessing reverses a specific restriction of excommunication: marital relations, social distancing, anointing, and footwear"}], :frame {:text "The tribe of Asher is associated with olive oil — Jacob blessed Asher with 'his bread shall be rich with oil' (Genesis 49:20) and Asher's territory was known for olive production. The restrictions placed on one who is excommunicated are enumerated in Mishnah Mo'ed Katan 3:1, which lists prohibitions including marital relations, anointing, washing, and wearing shoes. Serah daughter of Asher is credited in Midrash Sefer Ha-Yashar (Vayigash) with informing Jacob that Joseph was alive.", :sources ["Genesis 49:20" "Mishnah Mo'ed Katan 3:1" "Sefer Ha-Yashar Vayigash"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מבנים אשר יהי רצוי", :translit "mi-banim asher yehi ratzuy", :gloss "From sons Asher acceptable"} {:he "ר\"ת מאיר", :translit "rashei teivot me'ir", :gloss "initial letters Me'ir"} {:he "השמן שהוא מאיר פניהם", :translit "ha-shemen she-hu me'ir pneihem", :gloss "the oil that it illuminates their faces"} {:he "ומאיר למנורה", :translit "u-me'ir la-menorah", :gloss "and illuminates for the Menorah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "מבנים אשר יהי רצוי", :spells "מאיר"}], :frame {:text "Olive oil from Asher's territory was associated with illumination — both for personal use, as oil of gladness that lights the face, and for the Menorah in the Tabernacle, whose pure olive oil is commanded in Exodus 27:20. The tribe of Asher's olive oil production is indicated in Deuteronomy 33:24's phrase 'he dips his foot in oil' and Genesis 49:20's blessing of Asher.", :sources ["Exodus 27:20" "Deuteronomy 33:24" "Genesis 49:20"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Each phrase of the blessing reverses a specific restriction of excommunication: marital relations, social distancing, anointing, and footwear", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "מבנים אשר יהי רצוי", :spells "מאיר", :letters ["מ" "א" "י" "ר"], :by :selah, :order :in-order}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:41:37.271528139Z", :model "glm-5.2"}